course: dictionary
lesson: 4790
title: Humanism: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Humanism is a noun, a name for a way of thinking. Humanists believe people can live good, meaningful lives using reason, kindness and science, without believing in God or a religion. «Most faiths and humanism value honesty, kindness, care for the poor and the Golden Rule.» Here humanism sits next to faiths, so the sentence is comparing two ways of living that both care about kindness.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Faiths are religions, and the sentence says humanism shares values with them, so humanism is a way of life, not a religion. Test it: swap in "a way of living" and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Humanism also has a history meaning. About six hundred years ago, in the Renaissance, humanism was a movement that brought back the learning of ancient Greece and Rome and put people at the centre of study. Renaissance humanists studied old books and art.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is which. «A humanist wedding» is about a modern non-religious ceremony, while «Renaissance humanism» points to the old movement. Always check the words next to the word.
fact: Humanism is a way of thinking that uses reason, kindness and science to live a good life, without believing in God or a religion.
fact: A humanist is a person who follows humanism.
fact: «Humanist values» are things like honesty and kindness, which many faiths share too.
fact: «Renaissance humanism» was a movement about six hundred years ago that brought back the learning of ancient Greece and Rome.
fact: Humanists may hold weddings and funerals without religious words, and try to make the best of this one life.
exercise: «Most faiths and humanism value honesty, kindness, care for the poor and the Golden Rule.» What do faiths and humanism have in common? | *Shared values like honesty and kindness | Neither cares about the poor | A belief in many gods | Both are only found in history books
exercise: What does humanism mean? | Belief in many gods and religious words at every ceremony | *A way of thinking that uses reason and kindness to live a good life without religion | A movement that only studies maths | A type of school for very young children
exercise: «A humanist wedding» is different from a religious one. How? | *A humanist wedding has no religious words and celebrates this one life | A humanist wedding is always held outdoors in the rain | A humanist wedding is held only in a church | A humanist wedding has to be held in ancient Rome
test: «Some form of it is found in almost every religion and in humanism too.» In this sentence, what does it most likely refer to? | A famous Renaissance painting | A type of food eaten at weddings | *A shared value such as kindness or the Golden Rule | A rule about how to build castles
test: Does humanism need a belief in God? | *No, humanism is a way of living without believing in God or a religion | Yes, it always does | Only on Sundays | Only in Scotland, where it began
exam: Which sentence best explains humanism? | *Humanism is a way of living that uses reason, kindness and science, without needing religion | Humanism is a sport played in the Renaissance | Humanism is a type of weather found in Scotland | Humanism is a religion that worships many gods
